WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A trajectory is a sequence of vehicle poses, not just a line on the road.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
In a narrow passage, a small lateral change alters the remaining clearance.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Longitudinal changes alter the gap to the vehicle ahead at the same timestamp.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Start with an endpoint request. A native parent supplies the path in between.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Score the complete path, then store its utility at the terminal state it reaches.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Feedback from nearby reached states guides the next completion requests.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The archive uses position, heading and speed. Here we see its XY projection.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Each new request becomes a complete path before its utility enters the archive.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The accepted endpoint plan meets a native proposal from the second planner.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Bounded interpolation and geometric search establish a shared trajectory center.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Longitudinal, lateral and timing adjustments refine the motion around this center.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:38.000
One branch tests bounded blends with proposals from both frozen planners.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The control branch adds the bounded difference between two rollouts to the center.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Both branches start from the same center. Zero control change preserves it exactly.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Align the proposal and control trajectories at the same future timestamps.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:14.000
A temporal weight combines their contributions along the complete horizon.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Configured scorers compare each complete candidate with the current reference.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Select an admitted update, or retain the current reference when replacement fails.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Endpoint feedback locates promising motions. Local search refines their shape and timing.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Search the trajectory at test time. Keep the driving models frozen.
